course: dictionary
lesson: 7323
title: Sad sounds and feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Plaintive is an adjective. It describes a sound or voice that seems sad, like someone complaining or crying softly. In «His home had called him sorrowfully, reproachfully, but with no bitterness or anger; only with plaintive reminder that it was there, and wanted him», the reminder is not angry. It is sad and gentle, so plaintive fits.
explain: Look at the words around plaintive. Writers often pair it with sounds: a plaintive cry, a plaintive song, a plaintive voice. The clue is that the sound is soft and sad, not loud or cheerful. Ask yourself: what kind of sound is this? Then swap in sad-sounding and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, the Mole smells his old home and gives a plaintive cry. That cry is so sad and gentle that the Rat turns back. The author chose plaintive because it shows the feeling in the sound, not just the fact that a sound was made.
fact: Plaintive is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a cry, a song or a voice.
fact: «Plaintive» means sounding sad, like someone complaining or crying softly.
fact: «Plaintive» can also mean sad and gentle, asking for pity.
fact: «A plaintive cry» means a soft, sad cry, such as that of a lost kitten.
fact: Good clues for plaintive are sad feelings and soft sounds in the words around it.
exercise: «The lost kitten gave a plaintive cry from under the hedge.» What does plaintive mean here? | *Sad-sounding, like a soft cry for help | Very fast | Loud and angry | Happy and singing
exercise: «Her plaintive voice asked, "Please can I come too?"» What feeling does the voice show? | Bored and yawning | Excited and cheering | *Sad and gentle, asking for pity | Cross and shouting
exercise: Sam says plaintive means loud. Which clue in «The plaintive cry of the lost kitten was soft and sad» shows he is wrong? | cry | plaintive | *soft and sad | lost
test: «The wind made a plaintive song through the empty trees.» What kind of song is it? | *A sad-sounding song | A fast dance tune | A sad, gentle song | A loud, cheerful song
test: Mia says the Mole's plaintive cry was angry. Which words in the story show she is wrong? | quiet silence, nobody moves | *sad-sounding cry, the Rat turns back | angry shouting, the Rat runs away | cheerful singing, the Mole laughs
exam: «His home had called him with a plaintive reminder that it was there.» What does plaintive mean? | Angry and loud | Happy and funny | Fast and busy | *Sad and gentle, like a soft call
